<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 26.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to April 26.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to April 26 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week April 20-April 26</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,661,795 tns	178,748 tns    10.76 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,804,453 tns	205,936 tns    11.41 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,658,592 tns	182,479 tns    11.00 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to April 26</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    33,387,637 tns    3,648,354 tns    10.83 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    33,850,872 tns    3,669,054 tns    10.84 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    31,975,100 tns    3,411,734 tns    10.67 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 58 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 58 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
